# A CANDIDATE ENGINE: the live series and the three staged engine fixes
# (operator, 2026-11-24, relayed by München from the architecture session:
# "Do everything, also 721, everything, run unattended" — an engine build with
# the pool's refusal and the second signal's exit). Built on the node with
#   SERIES_FILE=deploy/localai/patches/staged/engine-fixes.series \
#     sh deploy/localai/llama-cpp/build.sh sycl_f16 <out dir>
# (and the live engine's INTEL_STACK), installed beside the live engine,
# gated, then swapped. A new engine is a new run of every model on it.
#   0012  GGML_SYCL_REORDER_EXPERTS, default 1 = today's behaviour: it rides so
#         that the expert-layout comparison on the 35B needs no second build
#   0013  a refused device-memory commit fails the request, not the backend
#         (localai-bugs.md B18/P14; the condition of `make_room = "page"`)
#   0014  a second termination signal leaves at once (B19/P15)
# When their card checks pass, the three move up into `series` and this file
# goes (staged/README.md).
